WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.552
- You've gotta be (beep) kidding me.

00:00:02.552 --> 00:00:03.512
(laughing)

00:00:03.512 --> 00:00:07.012
(playful xylophone music)

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.290
- I begged my brother for
a Furby, I begged him.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:19.302
And at the time they were so expensive

00:00:19.302 --> 00:00:22.654
and he actually got me one for Christmas.

00:00:22.654 --> 00:00:26.154
(playful xylophone music)

00:00:29.287 --> 00:00:32.494
- There was this one toy
that was called Sky Dancers,

00:00:32.494 --> 00:00:33.973
where you like pulled on this string

00:00:33.973 --> 00:00:35.588
and it flew up into the
air because its like,

00:00:35.588 --> 00:00:37.769
it had wings on the side that did this.

00:00:37.769 --> 00:00:41.079
- I just remember the
Furby being the thing.

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:43.544
I guess it's like the iPhone for adults.

00:00:43.544 --> 00:00:46.570
(bright violin music)

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:48.487
(paper ripping)

00:00:48.487 --> 00:00:50.320
- Oh my god, you guys!

00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:55.170
- (Laughing) Cockadoodledoo?

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:56.714
(paper ripping)

00:00:56.714 --> 00:01:00.760
- Oh my god, this is like
the true '90s version.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.664
- This is crazy.

00:01:02.664 --> 00:01:04.122
You're so huge!

00:01:04.122 --> 00:01:04.955
- Oh.

00:01:04.955 --> 00:01:07.788
(Furby squawking)

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.737
- Hi, you're so pretty.

00:01:13.737 --> 00:01:16.690
You have kind of '80s hair,
but you know, so do I.

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:19.614
- This is kind of cute because
I'm a little bit homesick

00:01:19.614 --> 00:01:20.957
and I miss my brother.

00:01:20.957 --> 00:01:22.864
So this is heaps cool.

00:01:22.864 --> 00:01:24.867
- I had no idea you were going to do this.

00:01:24.867 --> 00:01:26.540
(laughing)

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.641
- There's something about having a doll,

00:01:28.641 --> 00:01:30.427
and especially a life size doll,

00:01:30.427 --> 00:01:32.520
like, this is like your friend.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:34.024
This is the size of me.

00:01:34.024 --> 00:01:35.192
(string sliding)

00:01:35.192 --> 00:01:36.985
- Oh! (laughing)

00:01:36.985 --> 00:01:39.080
(hands patting)

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:40.797
- Oh no! (laughing)

00:01:40.797 --> 00:01:43.315
Oh no, come on, play. (laughing)

00:01:43.315 --> 00:01:46.555
- (laughing) So much is
flashing back to me right now.

00:01:46.555 --> 00:01:48.766
- I feel like six-year-old Daysha.

00:01:48.766 --> 00:01:52.005
- When I was a kid, I
definitely had her play like,

00:01:52.005 --> 00:01:54.032
different things, like,

00:01:54.032 --> 00:01:56.285
I would be like, today
we're adventure Barbie,

00:01:56.285 --> 00:01:57.917
we're going on an adventure.

00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:59.335
(string buzzing)

00:01:59.335 --> 00:02:00.955
- Oh that one's way better.

00:02:00.955 --> 00:02:02.322
Okay, we're doing that one again.

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:03.938
(giggling)

00:02:03.938 --> 00:02:05.009
- I would do her hair,

00:02:05.009 --> 00:02:07.081
'cause I always had this crazy curly hair

00:02:07.081 --> 00:02:09.686
and nobody ever had the same hair as me.

00:02:09.686 --> 00:02:10.956
- I just wanna,

00:02:10.956 --> 00:02:12.870
(playful xylophone music)

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:14.161
(laughing quietly)

00:02:14.161 --> 00:02:15.521
and go,

00:02:15.521 --> 00:02:18.928
(metal pieces clinking together)

00:02:18.928 --> 00:02:20.113
Is this the right way?

00:02:20.113 --> 00:02:22.040
I don't even know.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.841
(Furby squawking)

00:02:23.841 --> 00:02:25.864
(laughing)

00:02:25.864 --> 00:02:27.357
- That's my kid alright.

00:02:27.357 --> 00:02:30.520
- You did enable me to do a
lot of fun creative things.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:31.752
I made up stories for you,

00:02:31.752 --> 00:02:34.092
you got me through the
doctors office visits,

00:02:34.092 --> 00:02:36.859
so thank you for that, I
appreciate you for that Barbie.

00:02:36.859 --> 00:02:38.827
- What was so cool about these was that

00:02:38.827 --> 00:02:40.831
it gave you the chance
to look after something

00:02:40.831 --> 00:02:42.466
when you weren't allowed pets,

00:02:42.466 --> 00:02:44.688
or babies. (laughing)

00:02:44.688 --> 00:02:46.460
- Sky Dancers were one of
my favorites because like,

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:49.708
you could like control how high they went.

00:02:49.708 --> 00:02:52.107
- My brother and I still
talk about it to this day,

00:02:52.107 --> 00:02:54.251
'cause it was such a big
deal for him to spend

00:02:54.251 --> 00:02:57.327
that much money on a
Christmas present for me.

00:02:57.327 --> 00:02:59.109
- This is insane, this is like

00:02:59.109 --> 00:03:01.330
the greatest Christmas surprise.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:03.464
Gave me back a piece of my childhood.

00:03:03.464 --> 00:03:04.483
(slow piano)

00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:06.374
- It felt very, magical.

00:03:06.374 --> 00:03:08.965
Like Christmas magic, this
felt like Christmas magic.

00:03:08.965 --> 00:03:11.963
- I think that I've always
been like an independent person

00:03:11.963 --> 00:03:13.146
from the beginning, it's like

00:03:13.146 --> 00:03:15.608
nah mom, you don't have
to make food for me,

00:03:15.608 --> 00:03:17.807
I got this, I got my Easy-Bake Oven.

